Everything You Could Want to Know About Synths

THE BIG 3
1. Eurocorp (The Cybernetic-Organic Hybrid)
Construction: Uses highly advanced, proprietary Tier 4+ cybernetic internal structural components and mechanical systems, but wraps them entirely within a fully realized envelope of lab-grown artificial skin, complex subdermal tissue matrices, and fully simulated organic organ analogues.

2. Stellaris (The Advanced Robotic Android)
Construction: Utilizes a highly sophisticated, state-of-the-art robotic chassis built from classified lightweight alloys and neural-link components, covered flawlessly in premium artificial skin, tissue layers, and synthetic organs designed to mimic biology mechanically.

3. AMAC (The Bioengineered Synthetic)
Construction: Bypasses traditional mechanics entirely. AMAC constructs an actual, fully biological, vat-grown, bioengineered human body. This flesh-and-blood form is heavily enhanced with integrated biotechnology and directly controlled by an advanced, localized AI brain matrix.


TIER 1 SYNTHS

The Endoskeleton: Poly-Composite Matrix (PCM): Instead of heavy titanium or steel, the skeleton is injection-molded from a dense, high-grade structural polymer (similar to a 24th-century evolution of carbon-fiber-reinforced PEEK).
Properties: Non-metallic, entirely non-corrosive, lighter than aluminum, but with a tensile strength that easily matches structural steel.
Production: It can be stamped out or molded in minutes in a factory, keeping manufacturing costs incredibly low.

2. The Joints: Self-Lubricating Polymer Sockets: To keep maintenance low for the consumer, the joints don't use metal ball bearings or hydraulic fluids.
Construction: The joints are simple ball-and-socket or hinge configurations made of high-density, low-friction plastics (like an advanced Teflon/Nylon hybrid).
Vibe: They are completely silent when moving slowly, but under heavy loads or fast movements, they emit that faint, rhythmic plastic-on-plastic whir-click or a slight hydraulic-like hiss from the air displacement.

3. Internal Anatomy & Housing
Because the skeleton is hollow and molded, the "organs" of the synth are actually just modular plastic blocks tucked neatly inside the ribcage and pelvic cavities.
The Chest Cavity: Houses the central processing unit (the "brain" is placed in the chest for better structural protection than the head), the main solid-state battery core, and the cooling fans or heat sinks.
The Internal Routing: Channels are molded directly into the PCM bones themselves. All the wiring, power lines, and actuator cables run inside the skeleton, keeping the internal anatomy incredibly clean, organized, and easy for a basic technician (or a cheap street-modder) to swap out.

4. The Muscle Tech: First-Gen Electro-Active Myomer (EAM): Instead of heavy actuators at the joints, Tiers 1 and 2 use linear bundles of dark grey, rubbery polymer fibers that run parallel to the Poly-Composite Matrix (PCM) skeleton.
The Mechanism: When a low-voltage electrical current passes through a bundle, the polymer contracts instantly; when the current stops, it relaxes. It works exactly like a human biceps or hamstring.
The Look: If you stripped away the skin of a Tier 1 or Tier 2 synth, they would look like an anatomical model of a flayed human, but made entirely of tightly packed, fibrous synthetic rubber bands rather than red meat.

5. The Power Supply: Solid-State Density Core (SSDC): By 2319, standard battery tech has evolved past liquid-electrolyte lithium-ion (which degrades, overheats, and can catch fire). Instead, Tiers 1 and 2 use a Solid-State Lithium-Ceramic or Lithium-Sulfur Core.
Placement & Aesthetics: To keep the synth's center of gravity natural and human-like, the battery isn't a single clunky box. It is a flat, dense, curved block integrated directly into the pelvic cavity or lower rib cage of the Poly-Composite Matrix (PCM) skeleton.
Charging & Lifecycle: It charges inductively through a pad (like a smart mattress or a dedicated charging chair) or via a standard port hidden discretely on the body (like the lower back or behind the ear). At Tier 1 and 2 efficiency levels, a full charge gives the unit about 24 to 36 hours of continuous operational time before requiring a low-power "sleep/recharge" cycle.
The Weight Factor: Just like a modern EV or smartphone, the battery is actually the heaviest single component inside the synth. This works out perfectly for your stats—it gives both Tier 1 and Tier 2 a solid, grounded weight that contributes to their "High Human Average" Constitution.

6. The Nervous System: The Bus-Ribbon Neural Array
Instead of a complex, fragile web of millions of individual copper wires, a budget synth in 2319 borrows architecture from modern computing and flat-flex cables, but scales it to a human body.
The Spine Trunk: Running down the hollow center of the PCM plastic spine is a thick, flexible, heavily insulated flat-flex bus ribbon. This single trunk line acts as the central nervous system, carrying both high-voltage power from the battery and data signals from the processor in the chest.
Molded Channels: Branching off the spine, smaller flat-ribbon cables run down the arms and legs, tucked completely inside pre-molded tracks along the plastic bones.
Localized Nodes (The Motion Controller): To achieve that Humans-style movement, the nervous system uses a "distributed" layout. The central processor doesn't manage every single muscle fiber directly. Instead, it sends a general command (e.g., "Extend right arm") down the ribbon cable to a Local Node Cluster located at the shoulder or elbow joint.
The Voltage Threshold: This local node interprets the signal and shoots the corresponding voltage directly into the nearby myomer muscle bundles. Because these budget nodes process voltage adjustments in distinct, milli-second intervals rather than an infinitely smooth analog stream, it perfectly reinforces that slightly rhythmic, calculated movement cadence.

Passive-Vascular Dermal Layer
7. The Subdermal Matrix (The "Flesh")
Instead of real fat and muscle tissue, Tier 1 uses a mass-produced closed-cell hydrogel-silicone composite.
The Feel: This layer provides the anatomical "give" and soft resistance of human flesh. When you press into a Tier 1 companion's arm or thigh, it doesn't feel like hard plastic; it has the exact physical depth, squish, and weight of human adipose tissue and resting muscle.
The Function: It acts as a shock absorber to protect the delicate internal wiring and local node clusters, and acts as a barrier to keep internal mechanical heat from cooking the outer skin.

8. The Circulatory System: Thermal Regulation Loops
The Micro-Fluidic Grid: Embedded directly between the myomers and the subdermal flesh is a web of flexible, microscopic channels.
The Fluid: A cheap, non-toxic, highly thermal-conductive synthetic polymer fluid (colloquially called "blue-blood" or "coolant-plasma" because it glows a dull bluish-clear under UV light, differentiating it from the white blood of Tier 4s).
How it Regulates Temp: A tiny, silent micro-pump located next to the CPU core circulates this fluid. It pulls excess heat away from the battery and processor, routing it through the limbs and surface tissue. This solves two problems at once: it cools the internal electronics and naturally warms the synth's outer skin to a consistent 37°C (98.6°F), making them feel genuinely alive and warm to the touch.

9. The Surface: RealSkinn™ (2319 Consumer Grade)
The Material: A highly advanced, self-healing polyurethane-elastomer. It is entirely seamless because it is sprayed or molded directly over the subdermal matrix in the factory.
The Tactile Sensation: Thanks to centuries of refinement, it has a friction coefficient that perfectly mirrors human skin—it isn't sticky, slick, or oily. It feels soft, dry, and supple.
The Catch (Why it’s Tier 1): To keep production cheap, Tier 1 skin is cast from a handful of standardized, uniform master molds. While the material composition feels incredibly real, it lacks micro-details. It doesn't have true microscopic pores, shifting skin tones, fine vellus hair, or natural blemishes. It is a completely uniform canvas, which is exactly why manufacturers often choose the "Exotic" design path (fantasy or alien aesthetics)—it makes this flawless uniformity look intentional rather than fake.

10. Basic Sensory Input (The Nervous Loop)
By 2319, embedding a dense grid of microscopic tactile sensors is cheap. The skin of a Tier 1 companion can detect where it is being touched, the pressure of a grip, and ambient room temperature.
This sensory data is fed directly back into the flat-flex ribbon cables shown in edited-image.jpg, allowing the AI software to react smoothly and with emotional emulation to a hug, a caress, or a changes in environment.


TIER 2 SYNTHS

1. The Endoskeleton: Carbon-Reinforced Poly-Matrix (CRPM): While Tier 1 uses a mass-produced, injection-molded plastic skeleton, Tier 2 upgrades to a premium, high-density composite framework.
The Material: The core is constructed from a structural polymer matrix infused with woven carbon-nanotube lattices.
Properties: It is completely non-metallic, feather-light (weighing significantly less than Tier 1’s bones), but possesses a tensile strength and impact resistance that leaves structural steel and titanium in the dust. It absorbs heavy kinetic impacts effortlessly without cracking or warping.

2. The Joints: Magnetic-Fluid Acoustic Sockets: To achieve that effortless, silent Aliens grace, Tier 2 completely discards the physical friction of Tier 1's plastic ball-and-socket joints.
The Technology: The joints feature self-contained, sealed chambers filled with a specialized ferrofluid (magnetic fluid) and micro-magnetic stabilizers.
The Result: The physical bones of the joints never actually grind against one another; they sit suspended in a microscopic, pressurized cushion of magnetic fluid. Movement is 100% friction-free and entirely silent, eliminating any hint of a mechanical click or hiss, even when executing high-speed, intense physical maneuvers.

3. The Musculature: High-Density Carbon-Myomer Bundles: The muscles receive a massive architectural overhaul to support the synth's "Above Human Average" Strength and "High Human Average" Dexterity.
The Material: Instead of standard rubbery polymer strands, Tier 2 utilizes tightly wound, micro-braided carbon-fiber myomer bundles.
Density & Layering: The fiber count per muscle group is quadrupled compared to Tier 1. This allows for complex "micro-muscles" and stabilizers to be layered around the forearm, face, and fingers.
Performance: These fibers react exponentially faster to electrical currents. They pull maximum efficiency from the power grid, allowing the unit to move with instantaneous, organic acceleration, perfectly recreating human body language and micro-expressions without a shred of mechanical lag.

4. The Power Supply: Graphene Solid-State Density Core (G-SSDC). To feed the high-bandwidth processing and advanced myomer density, Tier 2 upgrades its energy grid to a premium power standard.
The Chemistry: A solid-state lithium-sulfur battery core utilizing graphene-matrix layers for hyper-efficient energy distribution.
Lifecycle & Longevity: This core holds triple the energy density of a Tier 1 battery in a footprint that is half the size, neatly integrated into the lower lumbar/pelvic region. A single charge easily grants a Tier 2 unit 72 to 96 hours of continuous, uncompromised operation before requiring a recharge loop.

5. Internal Anatomy & System Housing
The Core Shielding: The internal cavities (chest and pelvic regions) are lined with lightweight, shock-absorbing aerogel insulation. This ensures that even if a myomer muscle group is heavily strained and heating up, the heat is redirected entirely into the pressurized white coolant-plasma system rather than bleeding into the internal processing components.
The Nervous Core: The flat-flex ribbon cables are replaced by a Hyper-Bandwidth Optical Nerve Mesh. Strands of flexible, glass-polymer fiber-optics are braided directly into the carbon-myomer muscle fibers themselves, creating an instantaneous, bi-directional data loop between the central AI brain and the physical limbs.

6. Internal Refinement: High-Fidelity Voltage Trunks: While Tier 2 still uses the Poly-Composite Matrix (PCM) skeleton and Electro-Active Myomer (EAM) muscles, the infrastructure driving them gets a massive hardware upgrade.
The Component Upgrade: The Bus-Ribbon Neural Array is swapped for a high-bandwidth optical-fiber trunk. Instead of the local joint nodes processing commands in chunky millisecond "steps," Tier 2 nodes use continuous analog-voltage streams.
The Result: The muscles contract and relax with infinite, smooth precision. This allows a Tier 2 synth to execute complex, high-dexterity tasks—like playing an instrument, cooking delicate meals, or catching a falling object—with completely human-like reaction times.

7. The Soft Cover: Active-Vascular Layering: The passive cooling loops from Tier 1 are upgraded to an Active-Vascular System to support the much higher processing demands of the Tier 2 AI brain.
The Fluid: The coolant fluid is thicker, pressurized, and chemically identical to the milk-white synthetic plasma seen in the Aliens franchise.
The Function: A multi-chambered micro-pump in the chest dynamically regulates pressure. If the synth is running or exerting itself, the white plasma pumps faster, distributing heat evenly across the body. The surface temperature doesn't just sit at a static 37°C; it fluctuates naturally—becoming slightly warmer during physical closeness or high activity, flawlessly mimicking human biology.

8. The Surface: The Flawless "RealSkinn™" Matrix: This is where the engineering is incredibly advanced, yet reveals its commercial limitations.
The Material: High-grade, multi-stimulus RealSkinn™. The outer layer is packed with a hyper-dense grid of microscopic pressure, texture, and thermal sensors. A Tier 2 synth can genuinely "feel" the difference between silk, denim, a rough surface, or a gentle caress, and its body adjusts its touch dynamically in response.
The Aesthetic Flaw (The Uncanny Valley): To look human, Tier 2 synths don't use exotic molds like Tier 1. They are sculpted to look like beautiful, idealized humans. However, because this grade of skin is chemically infused with pigment and cast in high-precision corporate molds, it is too perfect.
The Details: There are no natural asymmetrical blemishes, no microscopic moles, no freckles, no tiny skin creases, and no faint vellus peach fuzz. Aesthetic features like lip coloration or eyeshadow are permanently blended into the elastomer matrix—meaning their makeup never smudges, fades, or alters texture.

9. Societal Impact
Under casual observation—passing them in a hallway, interacting with them at a store counter, or sitting across from them at dinner—a Tier 2 unit looks and moves like a flawlessly attractive human. But over an extended period of time, the total absence of human flaws, the un-smudging makeup, and the perfectly unblemished skin trigger a persistent, subconscious "uncanny valley" alarm in the human brain. They don't look like robots; they look like living statues.


